077 "selection" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436328 1078 #edb/ref 17592186436293 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436328 1079 #uuid "ec0f419d-2a0d-5de9-af19-f4de7b215052" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436329 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436290 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436329 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436303 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436329 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436314 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436329 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436318 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436329 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436320 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436329 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436329 1077 "selection" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436329 1078 #edb/ref 17592186436318 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436329 1079 #uuid "fb776df8-d18c-56c6-b0af-71e18ee9b2ff" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436330 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436328 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436330 1069 "q-159624" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436330 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436330 1071 "Find ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=x{e}^{y}+y{e}^{x}.$" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436330 1072 #uuid "7ea23849-68e0-52dc-ba91-b8da7ebd925a" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436330 1074 "The notation ${f}_{y}$ denotes the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y.$\n\nWe differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{y}+y{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{y})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{y})+{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\  & =x\\cdot {e}^{y}+{e}^{x}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =x{e}^{y}+{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436331 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436327 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436331 1069 "q-159609" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436331 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436331 1071 "For the function $f(x,y)=y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-2{x}^{5}{e}^{y},$ evaluate ${f}_{x}(1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3).$" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436331 1072 #uuid "90392678-f725-5c12-933c-87fa3256c47c" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436331 1074 "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-2{x}^{5}{e}^{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{5}{e}^{y}) \\\\  & =y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-2{e}^{y}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{5}) \\\\  & =y\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x})-2{e}^{y}\\cdot (5{x}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{x}-10{x}^{4}{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{1}-10\\cdot {1}^{4}\\cdot {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-10\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-30\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436332 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436326 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436332 1069 "q-159575" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436332 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436332 1071 "Given that $f(x,y)={x}^{y},$ then $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=$" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436332 1072 #uuid "9785714b-27e4-57d0-bac5-65edf8d118a2" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436332 1074 "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{f(x+h,y)-f(x,y)}{h}).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)={x}^{y},$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x+h,y)=(x+h)^{y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{(x+h)^{y}-{x}^{y}}{h}).\n$$" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436333 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436324 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436333 1069 "q-159612" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436333 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436333 1071 "Find $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ given that $f(x,y)=3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y-x{y}^{2}.$" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436333 1072 #uuid "ca64fedb-1539-5dab-a00d-8a624f81d8c4" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436333 1074 "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y-x{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y)-x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}-x\\cdot 2y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1+{y}^{2}}-2xy\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436334 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436325 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436334 1069 "q-159576" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436334 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436334 1071 "Given that $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{y}^{2}),$ then $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=$" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436334 1072 #uuid "ea65f87f-49a7-5b8c-93db-0d61d7663ef3" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436334 1074 "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{f(x+h,y)-f(x,y)}{h}).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{y}^{2}),$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x+h,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+h-{y}^{2}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+h-{y}^{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{y}^{2})}{h}).\n$$" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436335 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436329 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436335 1069 "q-159572" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436335 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436335 1071 "Given that $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy),$ then $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=$" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436335 1072 #uuid "fab082ec-08e1-574d-8102-367e3c718114" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true] [17592186436335 1074 "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{f(x+h,y)-f(x,y)}{h}).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy),$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x+h,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡((x+h)y).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡((x+h)y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)}{h}).\n$$" 13194139534795 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-04fd8c41-938d-5896-af76-a08ef933364a" 17592186436289 "answer-0966d4fd-1004-5375-90cf-1757ff705f99" 17592186436290 "answer-14ea137a-7846-516f-9915-09b5b41d82fc" 17592186436291 "answer-19821da5-f0d9-5231-b6e6-57d05a583c98" 17592186436292 "answer-21514dc3-fd5d-565c-a5dd-41b334024de1" 17592186436293 "answer-2a982a06-37f5-5503-bfa9-cb1dd6d38914" 17592186436294 "answer-31ac6394-634c-5df7-8435-c91eb48acad5" 17592186436295 "answer-3ca1bb65-4836-5031-98cd-687ce371b497" 17592186436296 "answer-3cd25198-8ccd-5ecb-ab36-bbba0fbb0d6d" 17592186436297 "answer-5347b519-c490-5531-86d9-c47823454ef5" 17592186436298 "answer-55c2293e-6cda-5e44-a3be-cf42f0b0106e" 17592186436299 "answer-58a19112-03ca-50b8-84a1-fe692ba95087" 17592186436300 "answer-60c0f614-7c90-5e8c-8d18-e07fc305806f" 17592186436301 "answer-642